Important Points:
Every Component in react maintains a state.You can put any variables to that state and Every  time you have to create local variables to use state inside react.So if i have to create a local variable in my component,then i have to create it by using useState hook . 

So if you have to create a local variable in react,you need to use  state variables like useState in react.These local state variables are created by using a useState hook.

What is hooks?
Hooks are nothing but  a normal js function.That is why we use brackets on every hook like useState(); Every hook in react has a special functionality for it. We can get useState function/hooks by react.This functions is written for us by a react/facebook developers.The basic functionality of useState function is to create local state variables.Basically useState function returns an array.The first variable of this array is the variable name.
import {useState} from "react"
const [namee]=useState(); //so we can say that namee is  a local state variable

So,in summary,
in normal js,we can create local variable like let namee="tayyab" while in react,we can create local variable by const [namee]=useState();

So if we have to update the namee state variable,react cannot allow us to directly update the namee.So useState array returns the second variable which is a function which functionality is to update the variable value.You can set his name whatever you want.
Below is a example:

import { useState } from "react";

 const Body = () => {
   const [namee,setNamee]=useState("kesa") 
    return (
      <>
      <div className="search-container">
      <input type="text" placeholder="Enter your value" value={namee} onChange={(e)=>{
        console.log(e);
        
        setNamee(e.target.value)
      }}/>
      <button>Search</button>
      </div>
      </>
    );
    export default Body
Imp Point:
There are 2 ways of array destructuring.One is ( const [namee,setNamee]=useState("kesa")) which is recommended .Another one is below
   or
   const searchData=useState("kesa"); 
   const [namee,setNamee]=searchData; //you can also destructure data like this    
  };
  
  Note:
  As we say it is a data destructuring then we cant destructure our data like this const {namee,setNamee}=useState("kesa").The answer is its a react developer choice.According to their recommendations,we have to use array destructuring instead of object destructuring for useState
