  Interview Question:
  We have a facility of local variables  then why we need state variables in react?
  let suppose we make  a local variable in react and we updated it in anywhere in app,in that case react does not show its updated value in ui because react does not keep a track of this local variables.React does not even know that  variable value has been created or even updated.React has not idea that what is happening with your variables even if you created thousand of variables.So if we want that react should keep a track of our local variables or  our local variables should always sync/connected with the ui ,for this u need to use state variables.When i updated my state variables ,it will automatically re render my component.Now question is what is happening behind the scenes when state variable is updated?The answer is when you created a state variable,react continuously watching that variable.So whenever my variable is updated,my whole component re renders( re renders means react destroys the whole body component and  creating the body once again.It is happening very fast.basically reconsiliation happening here)
  
  const Body = () => {
let username="tayyab";
    return (
      <>
      <h1>{username}</h1> //if username is updated anywhere in app,react ko pta he ni hu ga k username ki value update hu chuki ha 
      </>
    );
    export default Body
